[BEGIN]
  ObjTp=Hd
  Cmn1=UDP Extract Data v2.0\\\\Companion to UDP Broadcast and Receive||1
  Cmn2=v2.0. One instance latches IP, MAC, UID,\\and Data from the last||1
  Cmn3=inbound packet that matches this instance's filter, and\\drops that||1
  Cmn4=latch when the peer goes quiet.\\\\Wire Received_IP / Received_MAC||1
  Cmn5=/ Received_UID / Received_Data from the UDP\\module. Wire Packet_Rx||1
  Cmn6=to Packet_Rx. Do not wire Enable_FB.\\\\Packet_Rx evaluates the||1
  Cmn7=match immediately. The Received_* change path still\\waits 0.01||1
  Cmn8=s after the last change, so a v1.3 UDP symbol (no Packet_Rx) still\\
  Cmn9=works.\\\\Filter: Match_IP, Match_MAC, and Match_UID, each with||1
  Cmn10=a serial override.\\Default for every match parameter is [SKIP]||1
  Cmn11=(that field is not used).\\Any combination may be active. All active||1
  Cmn12=fields must match (AND).\\Exact, case-sensitive compare.\\\\At startup||1
  Cmn13=the locals take the parameters, then any override with length >||1
  Cmn14=0.\\CHANGE on an override sets that local to the override string||1
  Cmn15=as-is. An empty\\string means [SKIP] from then on and does not fall||1
  Cmn16=back to the parameter.\\\\A non-match does not clear a latch that||1
  Cmn17=is already held.\\Timeout is unitTime. 0s keeps the last match and||1
  Cmn18=leaves Online_FB high.\\Any other value drops Online_FB and clears||1
  Cmn19=the peer outputs when no new match\\arrives within that time. Default||1
  Cmn20=15s, maximum 600s.\\\\Peer_UID is Received_UID from the matching||1
  Cmn21=packet.\\Peer_Data is the raw Received_Data from the matching packet.
  Cmn22=\\\\Drop one copy of this symbol per peer.\\\\-- VERSION HISTORY||1
  Cmn23=--\\v2.0  2026-10-18\\- Packet_Rx evaluates the snapshot without||1
  Cmn24=the settle delay\\- Online_FB and Timeout. 0s latches until a new||1
  Cmn25=match. Any other time clears\\  the peer when packets stop.\\\\v1.
  Cmn26=0  2026-09-09\\- Prior symbol, left in the tree unchanged\\
[END]
